EmberBSD local adaptation, AI-assisted, 2026-10-07; not submitted upstream.
Lua 5.4 require returns loader data after the module value. Restrict the
version query to one result so stack-relative Lua/LGI version fields remain
correct. The upstream symptom is recorded in awesomeWM/awesome issue #3563:
https://github.com/awesomeWM/awesome/issues/3563

--- a/common/version.c
+++ b/common/version.c
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
         lua_pop(L, 1);
 
     /* Either push version number or error message onto stack */
-    (void) luaL_dostring(L, "return require('lgi.version')");
+    (void) luaL_dostring(L, "return (require('lgi.version'))");
 
 #ifdef WITH_DBUS
     const char *has_dbus = "✔";
